{
 "id": "lem-trf-affine-geometric-reducedness-criterion",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Geometric reducedness of an algebra is detected by the canonical algebraic closure",
 "statement": "Let $k$ be a field [def-pc-field-extension] and $A$ a commutative $k$-algebra [def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product]. Write $\\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure}(k)$ for Mathlib’s canonical algebraic closure. Then $A$ is geometrically reduced over $k$ (that is, $A\\otimes_kL$ is reduced for every field extension $L/k$) if and only if $A\\otimes_k\\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure}(k)$ is reduced.",
 "source": {
